  "notes": [
    "Draft: Stems: *bon-* and *ben-* (from the adverb *bene*, \"well\"). Languages: English, Spanish, Portuguese, French.",
    "Draft: *Melior* and *optimus* (the comparative and superlative of *bonus*) come from different roots, so *ameliorate, optimum, mejor, meilleur* do not belong here. They would make good puzzles of their own.",
    "Draft: Lookalikes to exclude: *boon* (a favor, Old Norse), *bond*, *bonfire* (\"bone fire\"), and *bonito* the fish.",
    "Draft: Uncertain and left out: English *bonny* (probably from French *bon*) and *boon companion*.",
    "Draft: The *bene-* words are compounds with *facere*, *dicere* and *velle* (*benefit, benediction, benevolent*), so they could also appear in puzzles for those verbs.",
    "Import: the draft lists “note bene”; corrected to “nota bene”.",
    "Import: Portuguese “bônus” is another spelling of “bónus”; kept as a variant."
  ]
}
